A||||5||Mark Matthews||Check engine light and ECM||||1||
Z||000000||Mark Matthews||12-09-2001||03:35 PM||||Okay, so I know that if the check engine light comes on you can check the ECM codes.  But, when do you check it?  If the check engine light is on all the time?  It popped on for like 5 minutes yesterday after I changed all the plugs, the back 3 I don't think have been chenged since '87.  The light came on and when i checked it it said 45 for rich exhaust.  But, now it doesn't come on anymore.  Does that mean the exhaust is okay?<P>I just don't know if I need to change my EGR and my 02 sensor if the light is no longer on.  I hunts at idle, but not all the time and not for very long.<P>T.I.A.<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<BR>'96 4x4 Tahoe<BR>'74 Wife, not happy about cars!  ;)||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnF||12-09-2001||05:00 PM||||FYI - I had the same problem.  Intermittant ENGINE light at any speed or condition.  Totally unpredictable.  I ignored it for a while.  No codes thrown.  <P>Eventually, I started getting a code 13.  I replaced 02 sensor and that was the end of the ENGINE light problem.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||johnt671||12-09-2001||05:15 PM||||If the light come on and then goes off the code is still stored in the computer and can be retrieved up to 50 starts.  If it come on and when off and stayed off I wouldn't worry about it.  Maybe when you you changed the old plugs the computer said "Wow, what happened? I'd better make the light come on cause I'm happy."||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||12-09-2001||05:53 PM||||Yep, sounds like an ECM brain fart.;<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||SKIDMARK||12-09-2001||07:40 PM||||Had the same thing happen with my 2.5 when I changed the plugs. The light would come on after that about once a week at freeway speeds. Every time, the codes were related to the O2 sensor (13, 44 or 45). I eventually replaced the O2 sensor and the problem went away. <BR>If it doesn't come on again ...it aint broke, don't try to fix it.<BR>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mark Matthews||12-09-2001||09:57 PM||||Sweet, thanks guys!  I'll see if I can get her to pass this week then.  I just need to change the oil first.<P>Do any of you guys use RedLine products.  I used it for just about every fluid in my BMW, 30 years old still running strong.  How much oil does the 2.8 take anyway?<P>Oh yeah... and you fill up the auto tranny thru the dipstick, right?  How much fluid for that one too?  Total change since RedLine is synthetic.  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top||||reg||1
